            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral chronic anterior uveitis &amp; neuro-ophthalmologic manifestations in a patient with Churg-Strauss syndrome: an unusual ocular presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with Churg-Strauss syndrome (CSS) who developed bilateral chronic anterior uveitis and neuro-ophthalmologic manifestations 20 years after the onset of asthma and sinus disease. The patient was treated successfully with a combination of cyclophosphamide and prednisone, after other immunomodulatory strategies, aside from systemic prednisone, had failed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
